MASTER PROJECT PROMPT — Organizational AI Support Desk & File Hub

1. Project Objective

Build a complete, secure, self-hosted Organizational AI Support Desk and Internal File Sharing System.

This is an independent web application, not a WordPress plugin and not an embedded chat widget.

The application will be deployed on a dedicated subdomain of the organization's main website, for example:

"support.example.com"

The system must provide four integrated workspaces:

1. Public Customer Support Portal
2. Operator Helpdesk
3. Shared File Hub
4. Super Admin Control Panel

Additionally, the application must include an AI-powered customer support assistant connected to an organization-managed Knowledge Base.

The AI assistant must answer customer questions using verified organizational knowledge, not general model knowledge or unsupported assumptions.

The application must be production-oriented, modular, maintainable, lightweight, secure, and straightforward to install, update, back up, and restore.

Do not build a toy demo or a visually attractive but functionally incomplete prototype.

---

2. Technology and Architecture

Use a Modular Monolith architecture.

Preferred stack:

- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- PostgreSQL
- Drizzle ORM
- Drizzle Kit for database migrations
- Better Auth for authentication and session management
- Zod for input validation
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui as the base UI component system
- A maintained real-time communication solution compatible with the selected architecture
- An AI integration layer supporting OpenAI-compatible APIs
- A document-processing and retrieval system for the Knowledge Base
- Docker Compose for deployment
- S3-compatible storage abstraction, with local persistent storage supported initially

Use stable, maintained packages. Before selecting any package, verify its current maintenance status, compatibility, security, and official documentation.

Do not introduce unnecessary microservices, Kubernetes, Redis, or additional infrastructure unless a demonstrated requirement justifies them.

The database must be the source of truth. All schema changes must be managed through version-controlled migrations.

Keep the application modular so that support, AI, knowledge management, file management, users, departments, permissions, notifications, and reporting can evolve independently without rewriting the core.

