5. Knowledge Base Management

The Super Admin panel must include a complete Knowledge Base Management workspace.

This is the official source of knowledge used by the AI assistant.

The Knowledge Base must support two primary methods of entering information.

5.1 Document Upload

Super Admin can upload organizational documents, including supported formats such as:

- PDF
- DOCX
- TXT
- Markdown
- Other document formats only when reliable text extraction is supported

The system must:

1. Receive and securely store the document.
2. Validate its file type and size.
3. Extract its text.
4. Process and normalize the extracted content.
5. Split the content into meaningful searchable sections.
6. Index the content for retrieval.
7. Associate the document with one or more departments or Knowledge Base collections.
8. Make it available to the AI only after successful processing.

Show document processing status:

- Uploaded
- Processing
- Indexed
- Failed
- Disabled

The Super Admin must be able to:

- View uploaded documents.
- View extracted text where appropriate.
- Edit document metadata.
- Organize documents into collections.
- Assign documents to departments.
- Enable or disable documents.
- Replace outdated documents.
- Delete documents and their associated search index records.
- Reprocess documents after changes.
- See indexing errors.

Do not silently treat failed or partially extracted documents as successfully indexed.

5.2 Question and Answer Entries

Provide a graphical Question and Answer editor.

The Super Admin must be able to create structured entries containing:

- Question
- Official answer
- Department or departments
- Category
- Keywords
- Status
- Last updated date

Support multiple alternative questions for the same official answer.

Example:

Question: شرایط ثبت‌نام دوره مربیگری چیست؟

Answer: The approved official registration procedure.

The AI must be able to retrieve these entries as authoritative information.

5.3 Knowledge Base Search and Retrieval

Implement a retrieval-based architecture (RAG).

Use a reliable retrieval pipeline with:

- Text extraction
- Document chunking
- Keyword or full-text search
- Semantic search when an embedding model is configured
- Metadata filtering
- Department-level filtering
- Retrieval relevance scoring
- Source tracking

Do not require a complicated vector database from the beginning if PostgreSQL-based search is sufficient for the initial scale.

The architecture must allow a vector search implementation to be introduced later without rewriting the Knowledge Base.

Every AI response must be traceable internally to the documents or Q&A entries that supported it.

Store the retrieved source references with the AI response for auditing and quality review.

Do not expose confidential internal document content or internal source metadata to customers unless explicitly approved.

5.4 Knowledge Base Access Control

Knowledge Base content may be:

- Global organizational knowledge
- Department-specific knowledge
- Restricted administrative knowledge

The AI must only retrieve content authorized for the current department and conversation.

A question asked through one department must not accidentally retrieve restricted knowledge from another department.

Only authorized administrators may create, edit, publish, or delete Knowledge Base content.

