The ticket detail view should show the full conversation, customer information, ticket metadata, assignment, and internal notes in a clear layout.

Internal notes must never be visible to customers or included in AI retrieval as public organizational knowledge.

7.3 Department-Level Access

Every operator belongs to one or more explicitly authorized departments.

By default:

- An operator can only see tickets belonging to their authorized departments.
- An operator cannot access another department's tickets by changing a URL or API request.
- An operator cannot reassign tickets to unauthorized departments.
- A department manager may have additional permissions within their department.
- Super Admin can access all departments and tickets according to system policy.

All access restrictions must be enforced by the backend, not merely by hiding UI elements.

7.4 Fair Ticket Distribution

Implement an automatic ticket assignment engine.

The system must support:

- Round-robin assignment.
- Least-loaded operator assignment.
- Configurable assignment strategy per department.
- Operator availability.
- Active/inactive operator status.
- Maximum active ticket limits.
- Manual assignment and reassignment.
- Automatic reassignment when an operator becomes inactive, where configured.
- Unassigned ticket queue.

The assignment engine must avoid repeatedly assigning new tickets to the same operator when other eligible operators are available.

Record every automatic and manual assignment in the audit log.

Assignment logic must be deterministic, concurrency-safe, and tested against simultaneous incoming tickets.

